{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-261", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/261", "wordCount": 2009, "segments": [{"start": 6.0, "text": "Hello. My name is Sommer"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "Panage and I'm an engineering"}, {"start": 9.0, "text": "manager on the Accessibility"}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "team here at Apple."}, {"start": 12.0, "text": "I'll be talking about the Large"}, {"start": 15.0, "text": "Content Viewer."}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "A feature that helps people who"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "prefer larger text sizes."}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "In this talk, you'll learn how"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "to ensure that all parts of your"}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "app are readable for everyone."}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "We'll first cover what the Large"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "Content Viewer is and why it's"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "important."}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "Next, we'll look at some API"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "that will allow you to support"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "it in your app."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "Finally, we'll cover examples of"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "some situations you might"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "encounter in your app and how to"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "handle them."}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "So let's start with some"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "background."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "Before we talk about the Large"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "Content Viewer, let's review a"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "related topic, Dynamic Type."}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "Dynamic Type is a feature that"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "allows you to customize the size"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "of text for the system."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "You can make it smaller if you"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "want to fit more content on"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "screen, or you can make it"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "larger and more readable."}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "By default, you can choose"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "between seven different sizes."}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "But if you go into your"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "Accessibility settings, you can"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "enable larger sizes and then you"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "get five additional sizes."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "This is important because many"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "people aren't just using this"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "feature because they prefer a"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "different text size."}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "They're doing it because they"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "need a larger text size in order"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "to be able to read the text."}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "So let's take a look at how"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "Dynamic Type changes the"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "behavior of iOS."}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "Here's how the phone app looks"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "at the default text size."}, {"start": 107.0, "text": "Now, if I change my text size to"}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "one of the Accessibility sizes,"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "the text gets much bigger."}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "However, you might have noticed"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "that part of the text on screen"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "is not getting bigger."}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "For example, look at the button"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "in the bottom left."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "If the customer has set their"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "size to be large like we see in"}, {"start": 128.0, "text": "the content area, then they"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "likely wouldn't see the text"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "that we see in the tab bar"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "because it's still small."}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "You might not be able to make up"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "the icon above it either in"}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "fact."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "However, we don't want to grow"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "the tab bar because that would"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "leave very little room for the"}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "main content that you see, in"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "this case your contact list."}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "So instead, if you're using"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "larger text sizes, we allow you"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "to long press on that button to"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "see a larger version."}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "Here's how that looks."}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "You can now drag your finger"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "along the bottom bar to see"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "what's on each of those buttons."}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "When you finally drag your"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "finger onto the button that you"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "want to tap, you can just let go"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "and the Apple act as though you"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "tapped the button."}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "This feature is what we call the"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "Large Content Viewer."}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "It allows people with low vision"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "to use tab bars or any other UI"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "that has to stay small."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "It's important for your app to"}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "show the Large Content Viewer"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "when appropriate."}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "If you're using standard UIKit"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "bars, you already showed the"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "Large Content Viewer."}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "You might just not have noticed"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "it before because it's only"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "enabled for the Accessibility"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "text sizes."}, {"start": 196.0, "text": "But if you've got a custom bar"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "or some other custom UI that has"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "to stay small, you'll need to"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "implement some API so that your"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "UI works just as well as the"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "standard UIKit controls."}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "Remember, this is only for the"}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "case when your custom UI cannot"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "grow in size."}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "Scaling with dynamic type is"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "always preferred to showing the"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "Large Content Viewer."}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "But sometimes, our bars simply"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "can't scale."}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "So let's look at how you can"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "support the Large Content Viewer"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "in your app."}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "Earlier, I said that you already"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "showed the Large Content Viewer"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "if you're using standard UIKit"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "bars."}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "But you might still need to do"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "something to make sure that it"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "looks good."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "If your bar items use PDF"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "images, make sure that you check"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "the Preserve Vector checkbox in"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "the asset catalog as seen here."}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "That will ensure that your"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "images scale smoothly to larger"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "sizes."}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "If your image button doesn't"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "have vector data, for example if"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "you're using a PNG, then by"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "default that image will look"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "blurry when it's shown in the"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "viewer."}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "To fix that, you'll need to"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "provide a larger version of the"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "image."}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "Use the large content size image"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "property on UI bar item to do"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "that."}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "If you need to adjust the"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "positioning, for example, if"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "your image doesn't look centered"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "in the viewer the way you wanted"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "to, then you can adjust the"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "large content size image in"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "sets."}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "So what do you need to do if you"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "have custom UI?"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "Well, before iOS 13, you"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "basically had to make your own"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "Large Content Viewer from"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "scratch."}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "But now, we've added API that"}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "allows you to show the same UI"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "that's shown for standard UIKit"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "bars."}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "So let's say you have a custom"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "tab bar, first you'll need to"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "specify the buttons in your tab"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "bar as items to be shown in the"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "viewer."}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "Then the Large Content Viewer"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "needs a title and/or an image"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "for each of those buttons."}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "If you happened to be using"}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "standard UIKit classes for those"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "buttons, you'll get those for"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "free."}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "Finally, you'll need to set up a"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "gesture interaction on the"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "custom tab bar itself."}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "The new UILargeContentViewerItem"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "protocol specifies the info that"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "the Large Content Viewer needs"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "in order to show your content."}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "This showsLargeContentViewer"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "property is what you'll use to"}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "mark your tab bar buttons."}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "Set it to true on any views that"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "should present the viewer."}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "Then you can specify a"}, {"start": 357.0, "text": "largeContentTitle and a"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "largeContentImage."}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "You can specify either of those"}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "or both of them."}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "If you want to reuse a PDF image"}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "from a small button, you can set"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "the scalesLargeContentImage"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "property to true."}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "But just as we saw earlier with"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "UI bar item, make sure that you"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "preserve the vector data for"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "your image."}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "And lastly, if you want to"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "center your image, you can use"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "the largeContentImageInsets."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "UIView already implements this"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "protocol and it also provides"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "setters. So in many cases, you can just"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "set the properties rather than"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "having to subclass and override."}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "Also, as we mentioned earlier,"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "certain UIKit classes like UI"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "button and UI label, return"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "default values for their title"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "and image."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "So that's how you annotate the"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "buttons in your tab bar."}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "Next, you'll need to add a"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "gesture interaction to the tab"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "bar itself."}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "To add the interaction, you'll"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "use the same addInteraction"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "method that's used for adding,"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "drag and drop support."}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "Here's how the interaction for"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "the Large Content Viewer works."}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "It's got a few properties on it."}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "In the simple case, you can"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "create an instance of this"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "interaction with no arguments"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "and you don't need to touch any"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "of the other properties here."}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "But if your app has other"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "gesture recognizers, you may"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "need to customize the behavior."}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "You can provide a delegate to"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "get fine-grained control over"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "how it works."}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "You can also use the"}, {"start": 452.0, "text": "gestureRecognizer property if"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "you need to set up relationships"}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "with your app's other gesture"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "recognizers."}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "Finally, to find out whether the"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "Large Content Viewer is enabled,"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "you can check the isEnabled"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "property."}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "And of course, you can listen"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "for the notification to see when"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "that changes."}, {"start": 472.0, "text": "There are a few ways to"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "customize the behavior using the"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "delegate."}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "First, you can specify what"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "happens when the user lifts"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "their finger from an item in"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "your custom view."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "It should act as though the user"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "tapped on that item."}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "If you don't implement this"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "method and you're using a"}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "standard UI control like UI"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "button, by default it will get"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "sent a touchup inside event."}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "But if you got something more"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "custom there, for example a view"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "with its own tap gesture"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "recognizer, you can implement"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "this method to provide the"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "behavior you need."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "Next, there's an option to"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "provide the item at a particular"}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "point. By default, the item will be"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "found by calling point inside"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "with event recursively on your"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "view hierarchy."}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "But that might not work if you"}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "aren't using views for example."}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "So, this method lets you return"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "which item should be shown in"}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "the viewer for a particular"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "point."}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "Finally, you can decide which"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "viewController should house the"}, {"start": 533.0, "text": "Large Content Viewer."}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "By default, UIKit will try to"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "pick a viewController that"}, {"start": 538.0, "text": "contains the view that you added"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "the interaction to."}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "But if that default choice"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "doesn't work well for your app,"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "you can specify one here."}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "So, we've covered the API."}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "Now let's look at some examples"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "showing how to use it."}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "First, let's look at a simple"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "case."}, {"start": 558.0, "text": "You've got a custom bar but"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "inside you've got standard UIKit"}, {"start": 562.0, "text": "views."}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "Here we've got a bar with a UI"}, {"start": 565.0, "text": "button and a UI label."}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "Because we're using standard"}, {"start": 570.0, "text": "views, all we need to do is up"}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "to the button and the label in"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "using the showsLargeContentViewer"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "property."}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "There's no need to specify a"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "title or an image since those"}, {"start": 582.0, "text": "can be inferred from the views"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "of the properties."}, {"start": 585.0, "text": "Finally, we can add the gesture"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "interaction to the custom bar"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "with no need to modify any"}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "properties."}, {"start": 591.0, "text": "That's it."}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "If your custom bar uses"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "something else for its buttons,"}, {"start": 597.0, "text": "then you'll need some of the"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "other API."}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "Let's say each of your buttons"}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "is an instance of a MyButton"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "custom class."}, {"start": 605.0, "text": "You can override the UI Large"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "Content Viewer item properties"}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "on your buttons to return the"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "right info."}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "Here we're returning true for"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "showsLargeContentViewer and"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "we're returning our text as the"}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "title."}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "If you have an image with vector"}, {"start": 623.0, "text": "data for each button, then you"}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "can use the exact same image for"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "the Large Content Viewer."}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "Just make sure to return true"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "for scalesLargeContentImage so"}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "that it grows to the correct"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "size."}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "Finally, let's look at an"}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "example when you need to deal"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "with another gesture recognizer."}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "A classic example from one of"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "Apple's apps is in Safari."}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "When you tap on the Back button,"}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "it goes to the previous page."}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "But when you long press on it,"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "it brings you to page with your"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "past browsing history."}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "The Large Content Viewer also"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "uses a long press gesture."}, {"start": 660.0, "text": "So how do you get those to work"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "together?"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "You should absolutely allow both"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "things to work."}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "In other words, let the Large"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "Content Viewer show so that"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "people can see what's on the"}, {"start": 672.0, "text": "button."}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "But once they've had a chance to"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "read it, do the thing you would"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "normally do on long press."}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "To do that, first, let's"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "increase our existing"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "longPressRecognizer's duration."}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "That way we'll give people some"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "extra time to show the viewer"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "first before we do the other"}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "action."}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "You should also make sure you"}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "update the duration if people's"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "setting change."}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "If they start or stop using one"}, {"start": 699.0, "text": "of the Accessibility text sizes,"}, {"start": 701.0, "text": "the duration should also update."}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "Next, let's set a"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "UIGestureRecognizer delegate on"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "the existing"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "longPressRecognizer."}, {"start": 711.0, "text": "Now, in your delegate callbacks,"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "you can make sure that both of"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "your existing longPressRecognizer and the"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "gestureRecognizer from the Large"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "Content Viewer can recognize at"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "the same time."}, {"start": 722.0, "text": "That way, neither one of them"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "will prevent the other from"}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "working."}, {"start": 727.0, "text": "Here, we can see the behavior"}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "with our Large Content Viewer"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "implementation."}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "If I lift my finger while the"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "Large Content Viewer is visible,"}, {"start": 736.0, "text": "I go back as expected."}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "However, if I long press for the"}, {"start": 739.0, "text": "longer duration, I can still get"}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "to that browsing history."}, {"start": 743.0, "text": "So that's how your app can"}, {"start": 745.0, "text": "accommodate people who prefer"}, {"start": 747.0, "text": "larger text sizes even for UI"}, {"start": 749.0, "text": "that needs to stay small."}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "Note that you should only use"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "the Large Content Viewer for UI"}, {"start": 755.0, "text": "that can't scale."}, {"start": 756.0, "text": "Scaling for Dynamic Type is"}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "always the preferred option."}, {"start": 760.0, "text": "So if you can do that, don't use"}, {"start": 761.0, "text": "this as API."}, {"start": 763.0, "text": "Finally, if your custom view has"}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "other interactions, make sure"}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "that those are all still"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "possible for people who use the"}, {"start": 770.0, "text": "Large Content Viewer."}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "That way, everyone can use all"}, {"start": 774.0, "text": "of your app's great features."}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "That's it for now."}]}
